we start this newshour with breaking  news from ukraine russian missiles have  hit a crowded shopping mall in the  central ukrainian city of kremen chuk  more than a thousand people are believed  to have been in the center at the time  of the attack charles stratford is  joining us right away from kiev to give  us an update on what you're hearing  about this attack charles  that's right horrific pictures that we  have begun to be uh seeing on twitter  and social media platforms of this  shopping mall reportedly hit by at least  one russian missile this afternoon as  you reported  the president actually has come out now  president zielinski has said that um  over a thousand people are inside or  were inside this mall  at the time this missile hit  um the city is interesting in as far as  what's happened there in the last few  days certainly yesterday  there was a russian attack on a bridge  in the city there was one person  confirmed dead in that strike another  five injured  certainly the ukrainian authorities are  saying that this shopping mall is  nowhere near any kind of strategic  institution or factory anything to do  with weapons  and it is a long way away from front  lines it's around at least 200  kilometers from the southern front line  probably a similar sort of distance from  the eastern front line it sits on the  denepa river  above the city of dunipro  so yeah we are hearing gradually of  reports of casualties as well  according to  a government source at least  two people have been killed so far and  another 20 injured  and of course condemnations are coming  through from government officials as  well um the head of the presidential  office describing it as basically  another russian atrocity russia should  be called to account  for this attack  of course russia has continuously said  that it has no intention of hitting  civilian targets and actively tries to  avoid them it was interesting yesterday  the missile strikes in in the capital  kiev they sunday morning very very early  very few civilians about but of course  there was civilian  infrastructure residential buildings hit  in that attack also so  yeah as i say horrific scenes of of fire  billowing smoke we're beginning to see  pictures also of the injured being  carried out of that mile um  horrific scenes  in that area cro-manchuk or that city  kromanchek which is effectively sort of  central eastern ukraine but as i say a  very long way away from front lines all  right charles we'll check in with you  later on thank you so much ross ratford  reporting for us from kiev
 

